# FigDown — figures as text. Spec: https://github.com/FigDown/figdown

figdown 0.1 table
# The DOCUMENT title, written empty (`EMPTY-LABEL-STATE`). This figure is named by the block
# caption below and by the prose that embeds it, so there is no second name to
# give — and `""` records that decision, where leaving the line out records
# nothing at all. The two render identically; the distinction is in the model,
# and a consumer that tests truthiness instead of key presence loses it.
title ""
table tb "Feature Matrix — rowspan/colspan merges with cell colors"
| Feature          | Cat A    | Cat B   | Notes         |
|------------------|:--------:|:-------:|---------------|
| Item 1           | yes      | yes     | baseline      |
| Item 2           | yes      | no      | cat-a only    |
| Item 3           | no       | yes     | cat-b only    |
| Item 4           | yes            || shared        |
| Item 5           | ^^             || shared        |
| Item 6           | —       | —       | none          |
# A row tint and a cell fill paint the SAME channel, so
# (`ROW-HIGHLIGHT-CELL-FILL-COLLISION`) a cell fill on a highlighted row is a line error rather than a
# silent override — the model used to say "row 1 is highlighted" while the
# drawing tinted only part of it. The highlights therefore sit on the rows
# that carry no per-cell fill; both features are still demonstrated.
cell 5 highlight
cell 6 highlight
cell (1,2) fill=#d1fae5
cell (1,3) fill=#d1fae5
cell (2,3) fill=#fecaca
cell (3,2) fill=#fecaca
cell (4,2) fill=#dbeafe
